      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Consistency is indeed key in many aspects of health and wellness; however, with warfarin, even a seemingly small or consistent ingestion of vitamin K-rich foods can significantly impact its anticoagulant properties. Your motivation to absorb vitamins is admirable, but this risk may overshadow the perceived benefits at the moment. It’s not just about keeping vitamin levels steady but also ensuring that the medication remains effective at preventing clots. For now, discussing your intentions with your doctor and possibly getting an updated plan that aligns with these goals will be the safest course of action to avoid unexpected issues with your therapy.",
      "source": "target",
